From b87964ccae22fb3b71d8588082027be8e709a8ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dru Satori <dru@druware.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:42:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/43] Network, NetworkStatus: show one entry per SSID

The Network preferences and the Deskbar NetworkStatus menu list one
item per access point, so a mesh or a multi-AP network shows the same
name several times, with no way to tell the entries apart.

Collapse the scan list to one entry per SSID before building the menu,
keeping the strongest access point of each (new
WirelessNetworkMenuItem::MergeSameName()). Hidden networks (no SSID)
stay one per BSSID. An entry is marked if any of its access points is
associated. In the preferences, items are matched by SSID and the join
message is updated to the group's current strongest access point.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Dru Satori <dru@druware.com>
(cherry picked from commit 19ee32ee04071f9ba70b10fdc5dbe7aa72805f31)
---
 src/apps/networkstatus/NetworkStatusView.cpp  |  2 +
 .../networkstatus/WirelessNetworkMenuItem.cpp | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../networkstatus/WirelessNetworkMenuItem.h   |  5 +++
 src/preferences/network/InterfaceView.cpp     | 24 +++++++++--
 4 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

